  "admissibility": "Finite values only, not assertion/cause proof; stage is preceding best-effort marker and can be stale/missing. Errors outside body/import/syntax/forcedexit may produce no file. Group may represent the latest loop context rather than unique failure provenance.",
  "additionalStageContract": "Failure-only metadata classification from captured original stable return arguments; exact raw equality required for pm-equal-call; parsed-equivalent unequal strings remain unclassified. Original assert equality/refusal unchanged. Detached16KiB each/64unionkeys; fixed group categories only, no raw field/package/value output. Outer stale/missing marker limitations remain. Multi-group stages encode exact seven-group membership/nonmembership/cardinality; normal-source integrity membership identifies differing integrity key. No rawvalues/package/path/exactkeycount/authenticatedsnapshot, staleouter retained. Encoding only existing groups uses captured size and at most seven has queries; faults preserve pm-multiple. No original object reread or metadata recomparison. Only completed current07 classifier result is refined: pm-07-v-yes means version own-presence/serialized-value contributes, pm-07-v-no means no version contribution and conditionally resolved contributes. Existing fallback stages carry unavailable, never negative. No actual version-string drift/cause/authenticated snapshot claim."
